<metadata_system id="057" name="WebP Metadata" category="IMG" category_label="Images" used_for="Modern web image format (WebP — Google, RFC 6386 base + container spec)" spec_source="Google WebP Container Specification + libwebp source (mux_types.h fetched 2026-04-30)" completeness="comprehensive" record_count="39">
  <description>WebP is Google's web image format combining VP8 (lossy) or VP8L (lossless) bitstreams in a RIFF container. Simple files are pure VP8 or VP8L; extended files use a VP8X header to declare additional capabilities (animation, alpha, ICC profile, EXIF, XMP). This entry covers all RIFF chunk types defined in Google's WebP Container Specification, plus the VP8 and VP8L bitstream headers that carry image dimensions, the ANIM/ANMF animation chunks, the ALPH alpha-encoding parameters, and the embedded metadata chunks that mirror what the JPEG/HEIF/PNG ecosystems carry.</description>
